srow(37, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"FOR THE LAND YOU ARE ENTERING TO POSSESS" (11:10) — THIS WAS SAID TO CALM ISRAEL AT THE HOUR THEY LEFT EGYPT, WHO SAID: SHALL WE NOT ENTER A LAND AS FINE AS THIS? THE ALL-PRESENT SAID: "NOT LIKE THE LAND OF EGYPT" — THE LAND OF ISRAEL PRAISED ABOVE IT. The head row of piska 37, THE FIRST PISKA ON THE CHAPTER — THE SIFREI OPENS ITS VOICE AT 11:10 after its silence over chapters 7-10 and 11:1-9 ({SP_(37, 1, "הרי", "זו", "נאמרה", "הפסה", "לישראל")} "this was said as a calming to Israel"; {SP_(37, 1, "מגיד", "שארץ", "ישראל", "משבחת", "ממנה")} "it tells that the Land of Israel is praised above it"): the verse read as REASSURANCE spoken at the exodus, the comparison with Egypt its praise. The English row carries the translator\'s own "(Dt.7:12)" for the portion\'s opening with his note that the Sifrei does not expound it (chapter 7\'s find — the interpolation, recorded there). The ink beside it: "not like the land of Egypt" one seat, "like the land of Egypt" twice in the Bible (Genesis 13:10 the other — computed). Read before at chapter 7 (the outside rows), REREAD WHOLE here in both files. No middah code (a narrative frame for the verse).')
srow(37, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'DOES SCRIPTURE PRAISE THE LAND OF ISRAEL OR THE LAND OF EGYPT? "HEBRON WAS BUILT SEVEN YEARS BEFORE ZOAN OF EGYPT" (NUMBERS 13:22) — ZOAN THE SEAT OF KINGSHIP (ISAIAH 30:4), HEBRON THE REFUSE OF THE LAND (GENESIS 35:27 — "MAMRE" READ "REBELLIOUS"): IF THE REFUSE OF THE LAND IS PRAISED WITH THE PRAISE OF EGYPT, THE FINEST OF ALL LANDS, HOW MUCH MORE THE LAND\'S PRAISE. The a-fortiori from Hebron ({SP_(37, 2, "וחברון", "שבע", "שנים", "נבנתה")} "and Hebron was built seven years"; {SP_(37, 2, "פסלת", "של", "ארץ", "ישראל")} "the refuse of the Land of Israel"; {SP_(37, 2, "קל", "וחמר")} "light and heavy"): I1 (qal wa-chomer (a-fortiori) — checked in MIDDOT.md before it was typed), the seven years of Numbers 13:22 the datum; the English\'s note names Genesis 13:10 for Egypt\'s praise (the kin the ink found — computed). Read before at a Genesis sitting (gen_29), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(37, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'AND IF YOU SAY: DID NOT THE ONE WHO BUILT THE ONE BUILD THE OTHER? — "THE SONS OF HAM: CUSH, EGYPT, PUT AND CANAAN" (GENESIS 10:6): HAM BUILT BOTH — AND ONE BUILDS THE FINE BEFORE THE POOR, FOR THE REFUSE OF THE FIRST GOES INTO THE SECOND; HEBRON, THE FINER, WAS BUILT FIRST. The parable of the two banquet halls ({SP_(37, 3, "ובני", "חם", "כוש", "ומצרים")} "and the sons of Ham: Cush and Egypt"; {SP_(37, 3, "משל", "לאדם", "שבנה", "שני", "טרקלינים")} "a parable of a man who built two halls"): E26 (mashal — checked), the order of building read as the order of worth. THE TWO FILES DIVIDE THE PISKA DIFFERENTLY HERE: the English\'s row 3 carries a paragraph of piska 39 (the mountain\'s thin soil, on 11:11 — 39:6\'s opening) and its row 4 opens with this Hebrew row\'s parable (asserted on both files; chapter 8\'s lesson a third time — the Hebrew\'s rows the addresses). Read before at a Genesis sitting (gen_24 — the table of nations), REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(37, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'AND SO IN THE WAYS OF THE ALL-PRESENT — WHATEVER IS DEARER PRECEDES ITS FELLOW: THE TORAH, DEAREST OF ALL, CREATED BEFORE ALL (PROVERBS 8:22-23); THE TEMPLE, DEAREST OF ALL, CREATED BEFORE ALL (JEREMIAH 17:12); THE LAND OF ISRAEL, DEAREST OF ALL, CREATED BEFORE ALL (PROVERBS 8:26 — "EARTH" THE OTHER LANDS, "FIELDS" THE DESERTS, "THE WORLD" THE LAND). The three firsts ({SP_(37, 4, "שכל", "מי", "שחביב", "קודם", "את", "חברו")} "that whatever is dear precedes its fellow"): the three nouns of Proverbs 8:26 assigned to three regions — the Land "the world" (the small type the English notes as lacking in many manuscripts, read and marked). Fresh in both files. No middah code (a mapping by proof-texts).')
srow(37, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: "THE WORLD" (TEVEL) IS THE LAND OF ISRAEL (PROVERBS 8:31 "DELIGHTING IN THE WORLD OF HIS LAND") — WHY "TEVEL"? BECAUSE IT IS SPICED (METUBELET) WITH EVERYTHING: EVERY LAND HAS WHAT ANOTHER LACKS, THE LAND OF ISRAEL LACKS NOTHING — "YOU SHALL LACK NOTHING IN IT" (8:9). The name read for its sound ({SP_(37, 5, "שהיא", "מתבלת", "בכל")} "that it is spiced with everything"; {SP_(37, 5, "אינה", "חסרה", "כלום")} "lacks nothing"): tevel / metubelet — chapter 8\'s row (read there on 8:9 and reread whole here), the name for its sound noted in MIDDOT\'s chapter-8 block without a code. The ink: 8:9 cited by name in both files (asserted). REREAD WHOLE.')
srow(37, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: "EARTH" THE OTHER LANDS, "FIELDS" THE DESERTS, "THE WORLD" THE LAND — WHY "TEVEL"? FOR THE SPICE (TEVEL) WITHIN IT: THE TORAH, "AMONG THE NATIONS THERE IS NO TORAH" (LAMENTATIONS 2:9) — THE TORAH IS IN THE LAND. The second reading of the sound ({SP_(37, 6, "זו", "תורה")} "this is Torah"). Fresh.')
srow(37, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'AND SO SENNACHERIB, COME TO SEDUCE ISRAEL: "UNTIL I COME AND TAKE YOU TO A LAND LIKE YOUR LAND" (2 KINGS 18:32) — NOT "A LAND FINER THAN YOURS" IS WRITTEN BUT "LIKE YOUR LAND": IF ONE COME TO PRAISE HIS OWN LAND DID NOT DISPARAGE THE LAND OF ISRAEL, HOW MUCH MORE ITS PRAISE. The a-fortiori from the enemy\'s mouth ({SP_(37, 7, "אל", "ארץ", "כארצכם")} "to a land like your land"; {SP_(37, 7, "קל", "וחומר", "לשבחה", "של", "ארץ", "ישראל")} "light and heavy to the praise of the Land of Israel"): I1 (checked) — the Rabshakeh\'s speech the datum (2 Kings 18:32 read as the Assyrian\'s own concession). Fresh.')
srow(37, 8, 'CONTEXT', f'R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: SENNACHERIB WAS A FOOL WHO DID NOT KNOW HOW TO SEDUCE — THE SUITOR WHO SAYS "YOUR FATHER IS A KING AND I AM A KING, YOUR FATHER FEEDS YOU MEAT AND FISH AND SO DO I" SEDUCES NO ONE; HE SHOULD SAY "YOUR FATHER IS A COMMONER AND I AM A KING, YOUR FATHER FEEDS YOU GREENS AND BEANS, I MEAT AND FISH, HE WALKS YOU TO THE BATHS, I CARRY YOU IN A LITTER" — AND THE A-FORTIORI AGAIN. The parable ({SP_(37, 8, "שוטה", "היה", "זה")} "a fool was this one"; {SP_(37, 8, "אביך", "מלך", "ואני", "מלך")} "your father a king and I a king"): E26 with I1 (checked). No citation in either file (asserted among the eleven). Fresh.')
srow(37, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE SIDONIANS CALL HERMON SIRION AND THE AMORITES CALL IT SENIR" (3:9), AND ELSEWHERE "MOUNT SION, WHICH IS HERMON" (4:48) — FOUR NAMES FOR ONE PLACE; WHY DOES THE WORLD NEED TO KNOW? BECAUSE FOUR KINGDOMS QUARRELLED OVER IT, EACH SAYING "LET IT BE CALLED BY MY NAME": IF FOUR KINGDOMS FOUGHT OVER THE REFUSE OF THE MOUNTAINS OF ISRAEL, HOW MUCH MORE THE LAND\'S PRAISE. Hermon\'s four names ({SP_(37, 9, "נמצא", "קרוי", "ארבעה", "שמות")} "it turns out to be called by four names"; {SP_(37, 9, "ארבע", "מלכיות", "מתכתשות", "עליו")} "four kingdoms quarrelling over it"): I1 (checked) on a datum of the book\'s own opening (3:9 and 4:48 the names, read at the first sitting). Read before at chapters 1-3 and 4, REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(37, 10, 'CONTEXT', f'LIKEWISE "DANNAH AND KIRIATH-SANNAH, WHICH IS DEBIR" (JOSHUA 15:49) AND "THE NAME OF DEBIR BEFORE WAS KIRIATH-SEPHER" (15:15) — THREE NAMES, THREE KINGDOMS QUARRELLING OVER THE REFUSE OF THE CITIES OF ISRAEL: THE A-FORTIORI. The second exhibit ({SP_(37, 10, "נמצאת", "קרויה", "שלשה", "שמות")} "it turns out to be called by three names"); I1 (checked). Fresh.')
srow(37, 11, 'CONTEXT', f'LIKEWISE "GO UP TO THIS MOUNT ABARIM, MOUNT NEBO" (32:49) AND "GO UP TO THE TOP OF PISGAH" (3:27) — THREE NAMES, THREE KINGDOMS: THE A-FORTIORI. The third exhibit ({SP_(37, 11, "עלה", "ראש", "הפסגה")} "go up to the top of Pisgah"); I1 (checked). Read before at chapters 1-3, REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(37, 12, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND I GAVE YOU A DESIRABLE LAND, THE INHERITANCE OF THE DEER OF THE HOSTS OF NATIONS" (JEREMIAH 3:19) — A LAND OF VILLAS UPON VILLAS FOR KINGS AND GOVERNORS: EVERY KING AND GOVERNOR WHO ACQUIRED NOTHING IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL SAYS "I HAVE DONE NOTHING". The villas ({SP_(37, 12, "ארץ", "שעשויה", "חוילאות")} "a land made of villas"; {SP_(37, 12, "לא", "עשיתי", "כלום")} "I have done nothing"). Fresh.')
srow(37, 13, 'CONTEXT', f'R. JUDAH: WERE THE THIRTY-ONE KINGS OF OLD ALL IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL? RATHER, AS THEY DO IN ROME NOW — EVERY KING AND GOVERNOR WHO ACQUIRED NOTHING IN ROME SAYS "I HAVE DONE NOTHING": SO EVERY KING WHO ACQUIRED NO PALACES AND VILLAS IN THE LAND. Joshua 12:24\'s count of kings ({SP_(37, 13, "וכי", "אחד", "ושלשים", "מלך")} "and were the thirty-one kings"; {SP_(37, 13, "כדרך", "שעושים", "ברומי", "עכשו")} "as they do in Rome now"). No citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(37, 14, 'CONTEXT', f'"THE INHERITANCE OF THE DEER" — AS THE DEER IS LIGHTER OF FOOT THAN EVERY BEAST, SO THE FRUITS OF THE LAND OF ISRAEL ARE QUICKER TO RIPEN THAN THE FRUITS OF ALL LANDS. The deer\'s first likeness ({SP_(37, 14, "מה", "צבי", "זה", "קל", "ברגליו")} "as this deer is light on its feet"). Fresh.')
srow(37, 15, 'CONTEXT', f'ANOTHER WORD: AS THE DEER SKINNED — ITS SKIN DOES NOT HOLD ITS FLESH — SO THE LAND OF ISRAEL DOES NOT HOLD BACK ITS FRUITS WHILE ISRAEL DOES THE TORAH. The second likeness ({SP_(37, 15, "אין", "עורו", "מחזיק", "את", "בשרו")} "its skin does not hold its flesh"); no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(37, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'AS THE DEER IS THE LIGHTEST TO EAT OF EVERY BEAST, SO THE LAND\'S FRUITS — AND IF LIGHT, NOT RICH? "A LAND FLOWING WITH MILK AND HONEY" (11:9): RICH AS MILK AND SWEET AS HONEY. AND "A VINEYARD IN A HORN, THE SON OF OIL" (ISAIAH 5:1): AS THE OX HAS NOTHING HIGHER THAN ITS HORNS, THE LAND OF ISRAEL IS HIGHER THAN ALL LANDS — OR NOTHING OF LESS WORTH THAN ITS HORNS? "THE SON OF OIL": THE LAND IS RICH. THE HIGHER THE MORE PRAISED — "LET US GO UP AND POSSESS IT" (NUMBERS 13:30), "THEY WENT UP AND SPIED" (13:21), "THEY WENT UP BY THE SOUTH" (13:22), "THEY WENT UP FROM EGYPT" (GENESIS 45:25); THE TEMPLE HIGHER THAN ALL — "ARISE AND GO UP TO THE PLACE" (17:8), ISAIAH 2:3, JEREMIAH 31:5. The piska\'s close ({SP_(37, 16, "שמנים", "כחלב", "ומתוקים", "כדבש")} "rich as milk and sweet as honey"; {SP_(37, 16, "ארץ", "ישראל", "גבוהה", "מכל", "הארצות")} "the Land of Israel is higher than all the lands"): 11:9\'s milk and honey the row\'s own citation of the chapter (asserted in both files — the piska cites 11:9 where its head is 11:10), the "going up" of the four verses the height read as praise; the English numbers this one Hebrew row 9-10 (the two files\' grains). The ink: "a land flowing with milk and honey" fourteen seats (computed). Fresh in both files.')

srow(38, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"IT IS NOT LIKE THE LAND OF EGYPT" (11:10) — THE LAND OF EGYPT DRINKS FROM BELOW, THE LAND OF ISRAEL FROM ABOVE; IN EGYPT THE LOW DRINKS AND THE HIGH DOES NOT, IN THE LAND LOW AND HIGH DRINK; IN EGYPT THE LOW DRINKS AND THEN THE HIGH, IN THE LAND LOW AND HIGH AS ONE. The head row of piska 38, the second on 11:10 ({SP_(38, 1, "ארץ", "מצרים", "שותה", "מן", "הנמוך")} "the land of Egypt drinks from the low"; {SP_(38, 1, "שותה", "מן", "הגבוה")} "drinks from the high"): the verse read as HYDROLOGY — the Nile against the rain, 11:10-11\'s contrast in the shelf\'s own terms (the English supplies "the Nile waters" and "the rains"). The ink: the two words for rain (computed — the book\'s מטר ("rain") against the flood\'s גשם ("rain")). Fresh in both files.')
srow(38, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'IN EGYPT THE EXPOSED DRINKS AND THE UNEXPOSED DOES NOT; IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL EXPOSED AND UNEXPOSED DRINK. The second contrast ({SP_(38, 2, "גלוי", "שותה")} "the exposed drinks"); no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(38, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'EGYPT DRINKS AND THEN IS SOWN; THE LAND OF ISRAEL DRINKS AND IS SOWN, IS SOWN AND DRINKS, DRINKS EVERY DAY AND IS SOWN EVERY DAY. The third contrast ({SP_(38, 3, "שותה", "בכל", "יום", "ונזרעת")} "drinks every day and is sown"); no citation. Fresh.')
srow(38, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'EGYPT — IF YOU LABOR IN IT WITH MATTOCK AND SPADE AND LOSE YOUR SLEEP, IT YIELDS; IF NOT, NOTHING. THE LAND OF ISRAEL IS NOT SO: THEY SLEEP IN THEIR BEDS AND THE ALL-PRESENT BRINGS THEM RAIN. THE PARABLE OF THE KING WHO GAVE ONE WELL-BORN MAN A SLAVE AND FED THE OTHER WITH HIS OWN HAND: EVERY LAND WAS GIVEN SERVANTS — EGYPT DRINKS FROM THE NILE, BABYLON FROM ITS RIVERS — BUT THE LAND OF ISRAEL IS FED BY HIM WHO SPOKE AND THE WORLD WAS: NOT AS THE WAYS OF FLESH AND BLOOD, WHO BUY SLAVES TO FEED THEM, HE BUYS SLAVES TO FEED THEM. The parable ({SP_(38, 4, "והמקום", "מוריד", "להם", "גשמים")} "and the All-Present brings them rains"): E26 (checked) — the land watered by God\'s hand, 11:12\'s "seeks it" read ahead; no citation in either file. Fresh.')
srow(38, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'R. ELIEZER, R. JOSHUA AND R. ZADOK RECLINING AT THE WEDDING OF RABBAN GAMLIEL\'S SON — GAMLIEL SERVES THE CUP, R. ELIEZER REFUSES, R. JOSHUA TAKES IT: ABRAHAM, THE WORLD\'S GREAT ONE, SERVED THE ANGELS THINKING THEM ARABS (GENESIS 18:2) — SHALL GAMLIEL NOT SERVE US? R. ZADOK: YOU HAVE LEFT THE HONOR OF THE ALL-PRESENT FOR THE HONOR OF FLESH AND BLOOD — HE WHO BRINGS WINDS AND CLOUDS AND RAIN AND SETS A TABLE FOR EVERY CREATURE. The wedding story ({SP_(38, 5, "הנחתם", "כבוד", "מקום")} "you have left the honor of the All-Present"): I1 (checked) from Abraham to the master; the rain God\'s table — the row\'s tie to the piska. Fresh.')
srow(38, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'DOES SCRIPTURE COME FOR THIS ALONE, OR DOES IT COMPARE EGYPT — THE REFUSE OF ALL LANDS — TO THE LAND OF ISRAEL? "LIKE THE GARDEN OF THE LORD, LIKE THE LAND OF EGYPT" (GENESIS 13:10): "LIKE THE GARDEN OF THE LORD" FOR TREES, "LIKE THE LAND OF EGYPT" FOR SEEDS. Lot\'s plain ({SP_(38, 6, "באילנות")} "for trees"; {SP_(38, 6, "בזרעים")} "for seeds"): the comparison\'s two halves divided — THE INK AGREES: "like the land of Egypt" stands at Genesis 13:10 and 11:10 alone in the Bible (computed), the shelf pairing the two seats. Read before at a Genesis sitting (gen_29 — the separation from Lot), REREAD WHOLE here. No code (a division of a verse\'s two clauses).')
srow(38, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'OR DOES IT COMPARE ONLY THE UGLY PART OF EGYPT? "WHERE YOU DWELT" (LEVITICUS 18:3) — THE PLACE YOU DWELT, "THE BEST OF THE LAND" (GENESIS 47:6). OR ONLY THE HOUR OF ITS SHAME? "FROM WHICH YOU WENT OUT" — WHEN YOU WERE THERE IT WAS BLESSED FOR YOUR SAKE, NOT NOW, WHEN NO BLESSING IS ON IT AS WHEN YOU WERE THERE. The two refinements ({SP_(38, 7, "אשר", "ישבתם", "בה")} "where you dwelt"; {SP_(38, 7, "במיטב", "הארץ")} "in the best of the land"; {SP_(38, 7, "היתה", "מתברכת", "בשבילכם")} "it was blessed for your sake"): Goshen the term of the comparison, 11:10\'s "from which you went out" (the clause\'s one seat — computed) read as the blessing that left with Israel. Fresh.')
srow(38, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'WHEREVER THE RIGHTEOUS GO, BLESSING COMES AT THEIR FEET: ISAAC TO GERAR (GENESIS 26:12), JACOB TO LABAN (30:27), JOSEPH TO POTIPHAR (39:5), JACOB TO PHARAOH (47:10) — HOW DID HE BLESS HIM? THE YEARS OF FAMINE WERE HELD BACK: "I WILL SUSTAIN YOU" (50:21) — AS THE SUSTAINING SAID THERE (45:11) IS IN YEARS OF FAMINE, SO HERE. The four descents ({SP_(38, 8, "ברכה", "באת", "לרגלם")} "blessing came at their feet"; {SP_(38, 8, "מה", "כלכול", "האמור", "להלן")} "as the sustaining said there"): I2 (gezerah shavah on "sustain" — checked; the Tosefta Sotah 10 parallels in the English\'s notes). Fresh.')
srow(38, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: THAT IS NO SANCTIFICATION OF THE NAME, IF THE WORDS OF THE RIGHTEOUS HOLD IN THEIR LIFE AND LAPSE AT THEIR DEATH. R. ELAZAR SON OF R. SHIMON: I PREFER R. YOSE\'S WORDS TO MY FATHER\'S — WHEN JACOB DIED THE FAMINE RETURNED: THE SANCTIFICATION IS THAT WHILE THE RIGHTEOUS ARE IN THE WORLD, BLESSING IS IN THE WORLD. AND THE ARK OF GOD AT OBED-EDOM\'S HOUSE (2 SAMUEL 6:12): IF THE ARK, MADE FOR NO GAIN OR LOSS BUT FOR THE SHARDS OF THE TABLETS IN IT, BROUGHT BLESSING, HOW MUCH MORE THE RIGHTEOUS, FOR WHOM THE WORLD WAS CREATED. The dispute and the ark ({SP_(38, 9, "נסתלקו", "צדיקים", "מן", "העולם")} "when the righteous departed from the world"; {SP_(38, 9, "לשברי", "לוחות", "שבו")} "for the shards of the tablets in it"): I1 (checked) from the ark to the righteous — THE FRAGMENTS IN THE ARK named as the ark\'s purpose (chapter 10\'s compile wrote them into the ark at the erection\'s day: the shelf here holds the Bavli\'s one-ark reading). Fresh.')
srow(38, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'OUR FATHERS CAME TO THE LAND AND BLESSING CAME AT THEIR FEET — "HOUSES FULL OF EVERY GOOD THING WHICH YOU DID NOT FILL, CISTERNS HEWN WHICH YOU DID NOT HEW, VINEYARDS AND OLIVES WHICH YOU DID NOT PLANT" (6:11). R. SHIMON BEN YOHAI: IS IT NOT KNOWN YOU DID NOT FILL, HEW, PLANT — YOU HAVE ONLY NOW COME? WHAT DOES "FILLED, HEWN, PLANTED" TEACH? YOUR MERIT CAUSED IT. ALL FORTY YEARS IN THE WILDERNESS THE LAND\'S PEOPLE BUILT HOUSES, HEWED CISTERNS, PLANTED FIELDS AND VINEYARDS, THAT OUR FATHERS FIND IT FULL OF BLESSING; "AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED" (6:11) — YOU, WHILE THEY WITHHELD FROM THEIR WIVES AND CHILDREN. "FROM WHICH YOU WENT OUT" — BLESSED WHILE YOU WERE THERE, NOT NOW. The merit that caused it ({SP_(38, 10, "זכותך", "היא", "שגרמה")} "it is your merit that caused it"; {SP_(38, 10, "כל", "ארבעים", "שנה")} "all forty years"): 6:11 cited three times in the Hebrew, four in the English (asserted at chapter 6, the row read there on the Shema\'s chapter); the stated-obvious read for its addition (no code — the registry\'s particles absent). Read before at chapter 6, REREAD WHOLE here.')
srow(38, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'DOES SCRIPTURE COME FOR THIS, OR TO COMPARE THE ENTRY INTO THE ONE WITH THE ENTRY INTO THE OTHER? IN EGYPT YOU WERE FOR A COUNT OF YEARS, SABBATICALS AND JUBILEES — SO IN CANAAN? "TO POSSESS IT": TO POSSESS IT YOU COME, NOT TO BE ON IT FOR A COUNT OF YEARS. BUT THE DIFFERENCE: THE ENTRY INTO EGYPT WAS OPTIONAL, THE ENTRY INTO THE LAND OF ISRAEL OBLIGATORY; EGYPT WAS YOURS WHETHER YOU DID HIS WILL OR NOT, THE LAND OF ISRAEL NOT SO — IF YOU DO HIS WILL, CANAAN IS YOURS; IF NOT, YOU ARE EXILED FROM IT: "THAT THE LAND NOT VOMIT YOU OUT WHEN YOU DEFILE IT" (LEVITICUS 18:28). THE LAND CONDITIONAL ({SP_(38, 11, "ביאת", "ארץ", "מצרים", "רשות")} "the entry into the land of Egypt optional"; {SP_(38, 11, "ביאת", "ארץ", "ישראל", "חובה")} "the entry into the Land of Israel obligatory"; {SP_(38, 11, "הרי", "אתם", "גולים", "מעליה")} "you are exiled from it"): the piska\'s close reads 11:10\'s "to possess it" as tenure without a term and the chapter\'s law ahead — 11:17\'s "perish quickly from off the good land" — as the condition; the fold\'s Leviticus 18:28 the proof. The compile\'s DATA (the land\'s tenure conditional — 9b). Fresh in both files.')

